# Create View Rule

Use when creating a new feature view in masterfabric_core or MasterFabric-style projects.

## Directory Structure

```
lib/src/views/[feature_name]/
├── [feature_name]_view.dart      # View class
├── cubit/
│   ├── [feature_name]_cubit.dart # Business logic
│   └── [feature_name]_state.dart # State class
└── widgets/                      # Feature-specific widgets (optional)
    └── [feature_name]_*.dart
```

## Step 1: Create State

File: `cubit/[feature_name]_state.dart`

```dart
import 'package:equatable/equatable.dart';

enum MyFeatureStatus { initial, loading, success, error }

class MyFeatureState extends Equatable {
  final MyFeatureStatus status;
  final String? errorMessage;
  final List<MyItem>? items;

  const MyFeatureState({
    this.status = MyFeatureStatus.initial,
    this.errorMessage,
    this.items,
  });

  MyFeatureState copyWith({
    MyFeatureStatus? status,
    String? errorMessage,
    List<MyItem>? items,
  }) {
    return MyFeatureState(
      status: status ?? this.status,
      errorMessage: errorMessage ?? this.errorMessage,
      items: items ?? this.items,
    );
  }

  @override
  List<Object?> get props => [status, errorMessage, items];
}
```

## Step 2: Create Cubit

File: `cubit/[feature_name]_cubit.dart`

```dart
import 'package:injectable/injectable.dart';
import 'package:masterfabric_core/src/core.dart';

@injectable
class MyFeatureCubit extends BaseViewModelCubit<MyFeatureState> {
  MyFeatureCubit() : super(const MyFeatureState());

  Future<void> loadData() async {
    stateChanger(state.copyWith(status: MyFeatureStatus.loading));
    try {
      // Fetch data
      stateChanger(state.copyWith(status: MyFeatureStatus.success, items: data));
    } catch (e) {
      stateChanger(state.copyWith(
        status: MyFeatureStatus.error,
        errorMessage: e.toString(),
      ));
    }
  }
}
```

- Use `stateChanger()`, never `emit`
- Add `@injectable` for DI

## Step 3: Create View

File: `[feature_name]_view.dart`

```dart
import 'package:flutter/material.dart';
import 'package:masterfabric_core/src/core.dart';

class MyFeatureView extends MasterViewCubit<MyFeatureCubit, MyFeatureState> {
  MyFeatureView({required Function(String) goRoute})
      : super(
          goRoute: goRoute,
          useSafeArea: true,
          horizontalPadding: const PaddingVisibility.enabled(),
        );

  @override
  Future<void> initialContent(MyFeatureCubit viewModel, BuildContext context) async {
    viewModel.loadData();
  }

  @override
  Widget viewContent(BuildContext context, MyFeatureCubit viewModel, MyFeatureState state) {
    if (state.status == MyFeatureStatus.loading) return const LoadingView();
    if (state.status == MyFeatureStatus.error) return ErrorHandlingView(error: state.errorMessage);
    return _buildContent(state);
  }
}
```

## Step 4: Register in DI

Run after creating cubit:

```bash
dart run build_runner build --delete-conflicting-outputs
```

## Step 5: Add Route

Register the view in your GoRouter configuration.

## Checklist

- [ ] State extends Equatable with copyWith() and props
- [ ] Cubit extends BaseViewModelCubit<S> with @injectable
- [ ] View extends MasterViewCubit<V, S>
- [ ] initialContent() calls viewModel init logic
- [ ] viewContent() handles loading, error, success states
- [ ] Use stateChanger() not emit
